# llama.SPY Game Genie v1 - template, not a live codebook.
# off is a displacement from the resolved symbol (0 = the symbol itself).
# fp=buildid:<gnu-build-id> must match the running module or the read is refused.
#
# Replace this file from your llama-server binary:
#   scripts/gen-gg-offsets.sh "$(command -v llama-server)" llama_decode
# The script uses nm/readelf. See docs/GAME_GENIE.md.
#
# Format: LLMS1|sym=...|off=0x...|width=N|type=...|fp=buildid:...|note=...

LLMS1

LLMS1|sym=llama_decode|off=0x0|width=8|type=u64|fp=buildid:REPLACE_ME|note=TEMPLATE symbol+0; regenerate
LLMS1|sym=n_past|off=0x0|type=u64|fp=buildid:REPLACE_ME|note=TEMPLATE displacement 0; set a real symbol
LLMS1|sym=predicted_tok_s|off=0x0|type=f64|fp=buildid:REPLACE_ME|note=TEMPLATE
LLMS1|sym=extra_probe|off=0x10|type=u8|fp=buildid:REPLACE_ME|future_key=ignore_me|note=unknown-key test; displacement 0x10
